   "text": "I read the macrocycle as a linear peptide (Gln, Lys, N\u2011methyl\u2011Trp) closed through a pyridine\u2013benzene thioether linker, with the three amino\u2011acid stereocentres taken from the wedges.\n\n**Residues, from the left of the drawing:**\n- **Gln:** the side chain is CH2CH2C(=O)NH2. Its \u03b1\u2011NH is alkylated by the CH2 on the pyridine 3\u2011position. Its C=O forms an amide with the Lys NH.\n- **Lys:** the side chain is (CH2)4NH2. Its C=O is bonded to the N\u2011methyl nitrogen of Trp.\n- **N\u2011Me\u2011Trp:** the side chain is CH2 to indol\u20113\u2011yl. Its C=O forms an amide with an NH that carries the benzylic CH2.\n- **Linker:** the pyridine carries the S at C2 and the CH2NH at C3. The S is bonded to a benzene ring that also carries Cl, the CH2NH group and a 4\u2011carboxyphenyl group.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** the bold wedges at the Gln, Lys and Trp \u03b1\u2011carbons all give the L (S) configuration. For Gln the wedged side chain leaves the implicit H pointing back. The priorities N > C(=O) > CH2 then run counterclockwise, which is S. In the SMILES this appears as `[C@H]` for Gln, because its ring\u2011closure neighbour is listed in a different order. Lys and Trp are `[C@@H]`.\n\nI wrote the SMILES with the Gln nitrogen closing the macrocycle by ring closure 3, and checked that the ring closures and atom counts match the drawing.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)CC[C@H]3C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc4c[nH]c5ccccc45)C(=O)NCc6c(Sc8ncccc8CN3)c(Cl)ccc6-c7ccc(C(=O)O)cc7"
